  ('Stems', 'retail', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 690901', null, 'Stems is a high quality florist.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/stems.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Studio 4 Hair', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 696521', null, null, 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/studio-4-hair.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Superdrug', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 720099', null, 'Superdrug offers a wide range of products and services. Healthcare Products: Superdrug stocks a variety of over-the-counter medications, vitamins, supplements, first aid supplies, and personal health care products. Beauty and Cosmetics: The store offers a diverse selection of cosmetics, skincare products, haircare products, fragrances, and grooming essentials for both men and women. Toiletries: Superdrug carries a range of toiletries including bath and shower products, deodorants, dental care products, feminine hygiene products, and toiletry accessories. Haircare: Customers can find haircare products such as shampoos, conditioners, styling products, hair dyes, and hair accessories. Baby and Childcare: Superdrug provides baby and childcare products including diapers, wipes, baby food, and toiletries for infants and children. Fragrances: Superdrug offers a wide selection of perfumes and aftershaves from popular brands. Travel Essentials: Customers can find travel-sized toiletries, sunscreens, insect repellents, and other travel essentials.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/superdrug.jpeg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Tait & Peterson', 'other', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 693010', null, null, 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/tait-peterson.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Taxi Rank, Victoria Pier', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, null, null, 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/taxi-rank-victoria-pier.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Dowry', 'food_drink', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 692373', null, 'The Dowry opened in June 2018. A light and airy cafe bar with Scandinavian influences in the decor and fantastic views out over the harbour area, this is a lovely place to go for coffee, lunch or just a relaxing drink. Off sales are available from a wide selection of speciality craft beers wines and spirits.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-dowry.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Grand Hotel', 'accommodation', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '07828 129158', null, 'In the heart of Shetland&rsquo;s capital of Lerwick, the Grand Hotel offers comfortable ensuite rooms, free parking and excellent service to guests year-round. With local shops, restaurants and bars on your doorstep, the Grand Hotel gives you a base like no other to take in all Lerwick and Shetland has to offer.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/grand-hotel.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Harbour Café', 'food_drink', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 695271', null, 'Currently open: 7am - 12noon Monday to Saturday. 8am - 12noon on Sunday', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-harbour-cafe.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Kildrummy Corporation', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 697444', null, 'In 1986 Ken Beer began writing cost control software for BP Sullom Voe. The oil terminal was one of Europe&rsquo;s largest, based in Shetland, a remote island half way between Scotland and Norway. The software was so successful that BP deployed it on multi-million dollar projects across the globe. Their cost of ownership dropped because it ran on IBM PCs, rather than the common mainframes of the day. In 1992, Ken met three friends near Kildrummy Castle in the Scottish Highlands, to found a company that would take cutting edge cost control solutions to some of the world&rsquo;s largest oil and gas projects. That night, Kildrummy&reg; was born. We soon opened offices in Houston, Texas, to service all the oil majors, independents and JVs who were rolling out Kildrummy&reg; software. Twenty-six years later, Kildrummy is still building flexible systems that fit our customers&rsquo; policies and practices, because we believe in exceptional projects and exceptional service. That&rsquo;s why our customers trust our software to manage trillions of dollars in project cost world-wide.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-kildrummy-corporation.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Lounge Bar', 'food_drink', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 692231', null, null, 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-lounge-bar.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Noost Bar', 'tourism', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 693377', null, 'Located in the heart of Lerwick, The Noost Bar is a welcoming spot to relax, unwind, and enjoy great drinks in a friendly atmosphere. Whether you''re a local looking for your new favorite hangout or a visitor wanting to experience Shetland hospitality, The Noost offers a warm and inviting space for everyone. With a well-stocked bar featuring a selection of beers, spirits, and locally inspired drinks, it''s the perfect place to catch up with friends or enjoy a quiet drink after exploring the town. Keep an eye out for live music nights and special events.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/da-noost.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Original Cake Fridge', 'food_drink', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '07833 62544', null, 'Bringing a taste of home baking into Lerwick town centre, The Original Cake Fridge is the perfect spot for something sweet. Alongside their famous cakes and traybakes, you&rsquo;ll also find tea, coffee, and a lovely range of gifts for all occasions. Whether you&rsquo;re popping in for a treat, a cuppa, or a unique present, The Cake Fridge offers a warm welcome right in the heart of the town.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-original-cake-fridge.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Queens Hotel', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 692826', null, 'On Lerwick&rsquo;s seafront, the former lodberries, turned hotel, offers comfortable rooms to visitors to Shetland in the heart of &lsquo;old&rsquo; Lerwick. With a view across Lerwick&rsquo;s harbour to Bressay, Queens Hotel offers guests the perfect location for those that want to take in all that Lerwick has to offer. The Hotel is a stones throw from the pier which makes Queens a great shore base for visiting crews. The hotel caters for all types of guests, those needing a town base for a couple of days through to those who are visiting longer term, whether that&rsquo;s due to work or longer family visits. The accommodation at Queens offers well appointed, quality accommodation to suit all. The accommodation comprises: 8 Single Bedrooms 6 Double Bedrooms 12 Twin Bedrooms 1 Triple Bedroom Each room includes: Ensuite Television WiFi Appropriate Working Space The Queens Hotel is currently underdoing refurbishment and we do not currently offer breakfast or restaurant/bar facilities. However, there are many shops, cafes, restaurants and bars along the street and we would be more than happy to make recommendations to make your stay in Shetland the best it can be!', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/queens-hotel.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Royal Bank of Scotland', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, 'https://www.rbs.com/', 'Banking Services Monday 09:15 - 16:45. Tuesday 09:15 - 16:45. Wednesday 10:00 - 16:45. Thursday 09:15 - 16:45. Friday 09:15 - 16:45. Saturday Closed - Closed. Sunday Closed - Closed.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-royal-bank-of-scotland.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Shetland Times Newspaper', 'other', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, null, 'The Shetland Times is Shetland&rsquo;s longest-running weekly newspaper, keeping the community informed with trusted local news, features, sport and opinion for over a century. Published every week, the paper covers stories from across the isles, alongside in-depth reporting on local issues, community events, culture and business. The Shetland Times plays an important role in supporting Shetland&rsquo;s communities by sharing stories that matter and providing a platform for local voices.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-shetland-times-newspaper.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Swan Trust', 'retail', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 695193', null, 'The Swan Trust was formed in 1990, and today is responsible for the operation and upkeep of the Swan. The main objectives of the Trust are: To encourage and facilitate interested parties and particularly young people to sail on the Swan. To teach and keep alive the techniques of sailing and working a traditional sail Fifie. To maintain the Swan as a viable charitable enterprise. The Swan Trust operate a number of on board sailings and activities throughout the year, for which tickets are on sale to the public. For a full list of trips and to book, please visit the website or Facebook page for details.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/swan-trust.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('The Wine Shop', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 693580', null, 'All your wines, spirits, extensive malt selection, and beers under one roof, all at keen prices. Serving Lerwick since 1985, service, pricing, and variety of stock always available; and if you have a favourite tipple we don''t have, ask us, and we will stock it for you.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/the-wine-shop.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Thule Bar', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 692508', null, 'The oldest bar in Shetland, a very popular public house situated on Lerwick&rsquo;s harbour front &ndash; keeping customers refreshed since 1895! A warm, welcoming bar serving very wide range of wines, beers and spirits including fine malts (ask for the menu) as well as freshly ground coffee. The bar has had a few name changes since a public house was first opened on the site. We understand it was first named the Seaview Vaults before the harbour, as we know it now, was built. It then became the Thule Refreshment Bar, around the 1895 mark. We know the bar lost its drinks license in 1920 when a Veto Poll in Lerwick returned a result that saw the town of Lerwick become &ldquo;dry&rdquo;. Just what were the folk thinking? We think they just sold peanuts and crisps for a few years during that great catastrophe! Lerwick became a &ldquo;wet&rdquo; town again in 1947 and The Thule Bar began to pour beer once more, we&rsquo;ve been keeping the good citizens of Shetland and our many welcome visitors refreshed ever since. Cheers!', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/thule-bar.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Thulecraft Ltd', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 693192', null, 'Thulecraft Ltd are the agents in Shetland for Honda Motorcycles, ATV''s, Marine and Garden Equipment. We are also agents for Yamaha Marine and ATV''s, Hyundai power products (Lawn Mowers, Generators etc) and Husqvarna lawn and garden products Our shop on Commercial Road also stocks a range of motorcycle and boating accessories. Our garage and stores at Gremista maintain and Services Motorcycles, ATV''s and Marine Engines. Our Factory at Gremista Manufactures Polysyrene boxes to service the local aquaculture industry.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/thulecraft-ltd.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Tooth and Nail Barber Surgeons', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 694054', null, 'Shetland''s Traditional Barber Shop Tuesday: 09:00 - 18:00 Wednesday: 09:00 - 18:00 Thursday: 10:00 - 20:00 Friday: 09:00 - 18:00 Saturday: 09:00 - 16:00 Sunday: CLOSED', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/tooth-and-nail-barber.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Universal Stores', 'retail', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 692138', null, 'Universal Stores brings together two lovely things in life, beautiful flowers and irresistible sweet treats. Whether you&rsquo;re picking up a fresh bouquet for a special occasion, a thoughtful gift, or just something to brighten your day, you&rsquo;ll find a great selection to choose from. Alongside the florals, you&rsquo;ll also discover a sweetie shop packed with favourites for all ages &ndash; from classic treats to fun goodies that make perfect gifts or a wee indulgence. Pop in for a browse, a chat, and leave with something that&rsquo;ll make you (or someone else) smile.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/universal-stores.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Vaila Fine Art', 'other', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 697374', null, null, 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/vaila-fine-art.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Venture Chiropractic & Sports Injuries', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, null, 'Chiropractors are spine and joint specialists who use their hands to treat problems in these areas. At Venture Chiropractic & Sports Injuries we''ll give you relief from back pain, neck pain and headaches. As well as getting to the root of the cause quickly, we''ll also give you postural advice and rehab exercises that will help prevent a recurrence of the problem. Not just backs! Yes, traditionally Chiropractors are considered the people to go to for back treatment but we also help with many other joint and muscle problems including sports injuries. As well as our Chiropractor, who has done extensive training in muscle release techniques, we have in-house services for Sports Physiotherapy and Massage Therapy.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/venture-chiropractic-sports-injuries.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Victoria Pier', 'other', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, null, null, 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/victoria-pier.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Virgin Money', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, null, 'With roots back to its establishment in Glasgow in 1838. Clydesdale Bank has a proud history of innovation and support for Scottish industry and communities. Virgin Money teamed up with Clydesdale Bank and Yorkshire Bank back in October 2018.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/clydesdale-bank-plc.png', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('VisitScotland', 'services', 'Lerwick, Shetland', null, null, 'Who we are We are Scotland&rsquo;s award-winning national tourism organisation. As a publicly-funded body (an NDPB, or &lsquo;non-departmental government body&rsquo;) we are accountable to the Minister for Enterprise, Energy and Tourism. Why we&rsquo;re here - the facts Our main aim to contribute significantly to the advancement of Scottish tourism by giving it a real presence in the global marketplace and benefiting the whole of Scotland. A strong and vibrant tourism sector is crucial for a successful economy. Currently tourism contributes &pound;11.6 billion to the Scottish economy each year (direct and indirect impact), as well as supporting over 180,000 jobs. In Shetland these figures are approximately &pound;16.5 million & 1200 jobs. As well as being a major employer in Scotland, the sector underpins the success of others such as transport, retail, farming, food and drink and construction.* * Deloitte study, 2013 Where we are Our local activities are organised around six regions and three island areas. In Shetland we have the Visitor Information Centres in Market Cross, Lerwick, & at Sumburgh Airport, plus the VisitScotland office above Market Cross. What we do Our purpose is to grow and develop the sustainable economic benefit of tourism to Scotland''s economy. This purpose is supported by five Corporate Objectives, which are closely linked: 1. Marketing: We will market Scotland and its outstanding assets to visitors from all parts of the world. This including the promotion of Scotland to people living in Scotland - encouraging them to visit different parts of the country 2. Information provision: We will provide information and inspiration to visitors both locally and globally via their preferred choice of medium (online, print, face-to-face) 3. Quality and sustainability: we will provide support and advice to businesses, with the goal of improving the quality and sustainability of the tourism sector in Scotland. We will provide assurance to visitors through our quality schemes. 4. Working in partnership: We will listen to and work with the industry, partners and stakeholders to shape our offering and support. 5. Events: We will maximise the benefits from the ''Winning Years'' and their legacy. We will implement the national events strategy, and sustain, develop and promote Scotland''s international profile as one of the world''s foremost events destinations.', 'https://oneshetland.com/business-logos/visit-shetland.jpg', 'livinglerwick', false, true),
  ('Westside Pine', 'retail', 'Lerwick, Shetland', '01595 696003', null, 'Giftware and furniture retail outlet, specialising in quality oak & pine furniture and funky gifts & home accessories. Stockists of Yankee Candle, Emma Bridgewater, East of India, Terramundi Pots, Alstons Upholstery, and many more!', null, 'livinglerwick', false, true)
